    "steps": [
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 61,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 62,
        "char_start": 0,
        "effective_step": 1,
        "end_token_index": 11,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 12,
        "step_number": 1,
        "text": "Step 1: Simplify the numerator and the denominator separately."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 240,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 241,
        "char_start": 64,
        "effective_step": 2,
        "end_token_index": 84,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 85,
        "step_number": 2,
        "text": "Step 2: For the numerator, use the product-to-sum identities:\n\\[\n\\cos A \\cos B = \\frac{1}{2} [\\cos(A+B) + \\cos(A-B)]\n\\]\n\\[\n\\sin A \\sin B = \\frac{1}{2} [\\cos(A-B) - \\cos(A+B)]\n\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 629,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 630,
        "char_start": 243,
        "effective_step": 3,
        "end_token_index": 268,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 269,
        "step_number": 3,
        "text": "Step 3: Apply these identities to the terms in the numerator:\n\\[\n\\cos 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ = \\frac{1}{2} [\\cos(25^\\circ) + \\cos(15^\\circ)]\n\\]\n\\[\n\\cos 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ = \\frac{1}{2} [\\cos(85^\\circ) + \\cos(15^\\circ)]\n\\]\n\\[\n\\sin 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ = \\frac{1}{2} [\\cos(15^\\circ) - \\cos(25^\\circ)]\n\\]\n\\[\n\\sin 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ = \\frac{1}{2} [\\cos(15^\\circ) - \\cos(85^\\circ)]\n\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 995,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 996,
        "char_start": 632,
        "effective_step": 4,
        "end_token_index": 444,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 445,
        "step_number": 4,
        "text": "Step 4: Substitute these into the numerator:\n\\[\n\\cos 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ + \\cos 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ - \\sin 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ - \\sin 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\frac{1}{2} [\\cos(25^\\circ) + \\cos(15^\\circ)] + \\frac{1}{2} [\\cos(85^\\circ) + \\cos(15^\\circ)] - \\frac{1}{2} [\\cos(15^\\circ) - \\cos(25^\\circ)] - \\frac{1}{2} [\\cos(15^\\circ) - \\cos(85^\\circ)]\n\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1120,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1121,
        "char_start": 998,
        "effective_step": 5,
        "end_token_index": 507,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 508,
        "step_number": 5,
        "text": "Step 5: Combine like terms:\n\\[\n= \\frac{1}{2} [2\\cos(25^\\circ) + 2\\cos(85^\\circ)]\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\cos(25^\\circ) + \\cos(85^\\circ)\n\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1289,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1290,
        "char_start": 1123,
        "effective_step": 6,
        "end_token_index": 579,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 580,
        "step_number": 6,
        "text": "Step 6: Use the identity \\(\\cos(90^\\circ - x) = \\sin(x)\\):\n\\[\n\\cos(85^\\circ) = \\sin(5^\\circ)\n\\]\nThus, the numerator simplifies to:\n\\[\n\\cos(25^\\circ) + \\sin(5^\\circ)\n\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1684,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1685,
        "char_start": 1292,
        "effective_step": 7,
        "end_token_index": 764,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 765,
        "step_number": 7,
        "text": "Step 7: For the denominator, use similar product-to-sum identities:\n\\[\n\\sin 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ = \\frac{1}{2} [\\sin(25^\\circ) + \\sin(15^\\circ)]\n\\]\n\\[\n\\sin 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ = \\frac{1}{2} [\\sin(85^\\circ) + \\sin(15^\\circ)]\n\\]\n\\[\n\\cos 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ = \\frac{1}{2} [\\sin(25^\\circ) - \\sin(15^\\circ)]\n\\]\n\\[\n\\sin 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ = \\frac{1}{2} [\\cos(15^\\circ) - \\cos(85^\\circ)]\n\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 2052,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 2053,
        "char_start": 1687,
        "effective_step": 8,
        "end_token_index": 940,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 941,
        "step_number": 8,
        "text": "Step 8: Substitute these into the denominator:\n\\[\n\\sin 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ - \\sin 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ + \\cos 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ - \\sin 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\frac{1}{2} [\\sin(25^\\circ) + \\sin(15^\\circ)] - \\frac{1}{2} [\\sin(85^\\circ) + \\sin(15^\\circ)] + \\frac{1}{2} [\\sin(25^\\circ) - \\sin(15^\\circ)] - \\frac{1}{2} [\\cos(15^\\circ) - \\cos(85^\\circ)]\n\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 2177,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 2178,
        "char_start": 2055,
        "effective_step": 9,
        "end_token_index": 1003,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 1004,
        "step_number": 9,
        "text": "Step 9: Combine like terms:\n\\[\n= \\frac{1}{2} [2\\sin(25^\\circ) - 2\\sin(85^\\circ)]\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\sin(25^\\circ) - \\sin(85^\\circ)\n\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 2349,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 2350,
        "char_start": 2180,
        "effective_step": 10,
        "end_token_index": 1076,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 1077,
        "step_number": 10,
        "text": "Step 10: Use the identity \\(\\sin(90^\\circ - x) = \\cos(x)\\):\n\\[\n\\sin(85^\\circ) = \\cos(5^\\circ)\n\\]\nThus, the denominator simplifies to:\n\\[\n\\sin(25^\\circ) - \\cos(5^\\circ)\n\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 2487,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 2488,
        "char_start": 2352,
        "effective_step": 11,
        "end_token_index": 1131,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 1132,
        "step_number": 11,
        "text": "Step 11: Now, the original expression becomes:\n\\[\n\\tan \\theta = \\frac{\\cos(25^\\circ) + \\sin(5^\\circ)}{\\sin(25^\\circ) - \\cos(5^\\circ)}\n\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 2720,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 2722,
        "char_start": 2490,
        "effective_step": 12,
        "end_token_index": 1213,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 1214,
        "step_number": 12,
        "text": "Step 12: Recognize that this is in the form of the tangent addition formula:\n\\[\n\\tan \\left( \\alpha + \\beta \\right) = \\frac{\\tan \\alpha + \\tan \\beta}{1 - \\tan \\alpha \\tan \\beta}\n\\]\nwhere \\(\\alpha = 25^\\circ\\) and \\(\\beta = 5^\\circ\\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 2813,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 2814,
        "char_start": 2724,
        "effective_step": 13,
        "end_token_index": 1254,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 1255,
        "step_number": 13,
        "text": "Step 13: Therefore, we have:\n\\[\n\\tan \\theta = \\tan (25^\\circ + 5^\\circ) = \\tan 30^\\circ\n\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 2929,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 2930,
        "char_start": 2816,
        "effective_step": 14,
        "end_token_index": 1298,
        "near_end": true,
        "prefix_token_count": 1299,
        "step_number": 14,
        "text": "Step 14: The least positive angle \\(\\theta\\) for which \\(\\tan \\theta = \\tan 30^\\circ\\) is:\n\\[\n\\theta = 30^\\circ\n\\]"
      }
    ]
