  "raw_text": "Step 1: Simplify the numerator and the denominator separately.\n\nStep 2: For the numerator, use the product-to-sum identities:\n\\[\n\\cos A \\cos B = \\frac{1}{2} [\\cos(A+B) + \\cos(A-B)]\n\\]\n\\[\n\\sin A \\sin B = \\frac{1}{2} [\\cos(A-B) - \\cos(A+B)]\n\\]\n\nStep 3: Apply these identities to the terms in the numerator:\n\\[\n\\cos 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ = \\frac{1}{2} [\\cos(25^\\circ) + \\cos(15^\\circ)]\n\\]\n\\[\n\\cos 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ = \\frac{1}{2} [\\cos(85^\\circ) + \\cos(15^\\circ)]\n\\]\n\\[\n\\sin 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ = \\frac{1}{2} [\\cos(15^\\circ) - \\cos(25^\\circ)]\n\\]\n\\[\n\\sin 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ = \\frac{1}{2} [\\cos(15^\\circ) - \\cos(85^\\circ)]\n\\]\n\nStep 4: Substitute these into the numerator:\n\\[\n\\cos 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ + \\cos 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ - \\sin 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ - \\sin 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\frac{1}{2} [\\cos(25^\\circ) + \\cos(15^\\circ)] + \\frac{1}{2} [\\cos(85^\\circ) + \\cos(15^\\circ)] - \\frac{1}{2} [\\cos(15^\\circ) - \\cos(25^\\circ)] - \\frac{1}{2} [\\cos(15^\\circ) - \\cos(85^\\circ)]\n\\]\n\nStep 5: Combine like terms:\n\\[\n= \\frac{1}{2} [2\\cos(25^\\circ) + 2\\cos(85^\\circ)]\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\cos(25^\\circ) + \\cos(85^\\circ)\n\\]\n\nStep 6: Use the identity \\(\\cos(90^\\circ - x) = \\sin(x)\\):\n\\[\n\\cos(85^\\circ) = \\sin(5^\\circ)\n\\]\nThus, the numerator simplifies to:\n\\[\n\\cos(25^\\circ) + \\sin(5^\\circ)\n\\]\n\nStep 7: For the denominator, use similar product-to-sum identities:\n\\[\n\\sin 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ = \\frac{1}{2} [\\sin(25^\\circ) + \\sin(15^\\circ)]\n\\]\n\\[\n\\sin 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ = \\frac{1}{2} [\\sin(85^\\circ) + \\sin(15^\\circ)]\n\\]\n\\[\n\\cos 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ = \\frac{1}{2} [\\sin(25^\\circ) - \\sin(15^\\circ)]\n\\]\n\\[\n\\sin 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ = \\frac{1}{2} [\\cos(15^\\circ) - \\cos(85^\\circ)]\n\\]\n\nStep 8: Substitute these into the denominator:\n\\[\n\\sin 5^\\circ \\cos 20^\\circ - \\sin 35^\\circ \\cos 50^\\circ + \\cos 5^\\circ \\sin 20^\\circ - \\sin 35^\\circ \\sin 50^\\circ\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\frac{1}{2} [\\sin(25^\\circ) + \\sin(15^\\circ)] - \\frac{1}{2} [\\sin(85^\\circ) + \\sin(15^\\circ)] + \\frac{1}{2} [\\sin(25^\\circ) - \\sin(15^\\circ)] - \\frac{1}{2} [\\cos(15^\\circ) - \\cos(85^\\circ)]\n\\]\n\nStep 9: Combine like terms:\n\\[\n= \\frac{1}{2} [2\\sin(25^\\circ) - 2\\sin(85^\\circ)]\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\sin(25^\\circ) - \\sin(85^\\circ)\n\\]\n\nStep 10: Use the identity \\(\\sin(90^\\circ - x) = \\cos(x)\\):\n\\[\n\\sin(85^\\circ) = \\cos(5^\\circ)\n\\]\nThus, the denominator simplifies to:\n\\[\n\\sin(25^\\circ) - \\cos(5^\\circ)\n\\]\n\nStep 11: Now, the original expression becomes:\n\\[\n\\tan \\theta = \\frac{\\cos(25^\\circ) + \\sin(5^\\circ)}{\\sin(25^\\circ) - \\cos(5^\\circ)}\n\\]\n\nStep 12: Recognize that this is in the form of the tangent addition formula:\n\\[\n\\tan \\left( \\alpha + \\beta \\right) = \\frac{\\tan \\alpha + \\tan \\beta}{1 - \\tan \\alpha \\tan \\beta}\n\\]\nwhere \\(\\alpha = 25^\\circ\\) and \\(\\beta = 5^\\circ\\).\n\nStep 13: Therefore, we have:\n\\[\n\\tan \\theta = \\tan (25^\\circ + 5^\\circ) = \\tan 30^\\circ\n\\]\n\nStep 14: The least positive angle \\(\\theta\\) for which \\(\\tan \\theta = \\tan 30^\\circ\\) is:\n\\[\n\\theta = 30^\\circ\n\\]\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{30}<|im_end|>",
